{
  "rationale": "The plant models the robot's motion and perception interface, separating motion commands from sensor outcomes. The specification enforces safe, coverage-oriented exploration: random_walk is used in clear states, move_forward is used for short progress, and obstacle events trigger conservative, deterministic turn or scan recovery before returning to exploration. Each obstacle state enables only a single recovery action, and full_rotate is reserved for dead-end recovery. All uncontrollables are total in every state, and the policy avoids oscillations and infinite controllable loops.",
